WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.760
A swarm of bloodthirsty entities waits outside&nbsp;
the protective boundary that surrounds the solar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:10.960
system. They surge through the vacuum of space&nbsp;
looking for vulnerabilities in the force field&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:15.280
that protects us from their destructive&nbsp;
powers. The creatures ram themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:21.200
against the barrier again and again, trying&nbsp;
to break through. Upon impact the forcefield&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:28.160
shimmers a golden color and displays a series of&nbsp;
thaumaturgical symbols, but it holds. Suddenly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.840
something flies through the protective shield&nbsp;
from inside the solar system; it leaves a hole.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:41.280
Two creatures enter our solar system before the&nbsp;
shield closes. This may be the end for humanity.&nbsp;

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.840
The Sixth Overseer sits at a computer&nbsp;
terminal massaging the bridge of his nose.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.600
He has just logged into the Foundation&nbsp;
database to gather information on an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:56.160
anomaly whose intentions are still unknown. The O5&nbsp;
Council wants him to vote on an extreme measure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:02.240
but he requires more information first. There is&nbsp;
something coming, he can feel it, and he thinks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:09.280
it has something to do with SCP-1548.
O5-6 straightens his back and sits up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:15.920
in his chair. He logs back into the Foundation&nbsp;
database and brings up the entry for SCP-1548.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.320
He knows that this SCP has been connected&nbsp;
to some odd occurrences recently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:25.840
but what are its true intentions? Is&nbsp;
SCP-1548 trying to help save the universe?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:33.200
Or is it a malicious entity hell bent&nbsp;
on destroying it? O5-6 must find out.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:40.000
He scrolls through the first few entries. SCP-1548&nbsp;
itself is a series of solar phenomena that occur&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.800
at the south pole of the sun. During&nbsp;
these events the sun's plasma morphs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:50.880
into different thaumaturgical symbols. Each&nbsp;
symbol is tens of thousands of miles across.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.040
The symbols themselves have not all&nbsp;
been classified by the Foundation yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.880
but, there are three that have&nbsp;
been observed multiple times.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:03.600
The first is unnamed symbol that, when&nbsp;
inscribed on a telescopic device by a person&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:10.080
with thaumaturgic abilities, can identify psionic&nbsp;
entities with malicious intents. The second symbol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:15.920
is known as the Kalaphastian Isle, which when&nbsp;
displayed on a material, strengthens it immensely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:21.040
and gives it the ability to absorb kinetic&nbsp;
and electromagnetic energy. The final symbol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:26.720
is the 12 Holy Owls of Serrinithium. When this&nbsp;
symbol is affixed to an object any entity that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:31.600
is killed by it will immediately annihilate&nbsp;
and take everything in its radius with it.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:36.720
O5-6 jots a note on the pad of paper sitting&nbsp;
on his desk. He has seen some of these symbols&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:41.440
before; they are connected to the Ortothan&nbsp;
mythology. The practitioners of this religion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:46.640
are known as the The Church of the Second Hytoth&nbsp;
and are a mix of human and alien entities whose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:52.160
main purpose is to aid the guardian deity of the&nbsp;
universe, "Rakmou-leusan," in combating any threat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:56.160
that may try to wipe out this existence.
There must be a connection between The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:04.080
Church of the Second Hytoth and SCP-1548, O5-6&nbsp;
thinks. He scrolls back through the SCP-1548&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:11.760
file to the entry logged on May 17, 1983, the&nbsp;
first time an event connected to SCP-1548 was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:17.360
recorded. A probe picked up the manifestation of&nbsp;
thaumaturgic symbols on the south pole of the sun.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:22.080
It was odd, but nothing other than the&nbsp;
manifestation of the symbols seemed to occur.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:29.520
This event was recorded as Extranormal Event-9008&nbsp;
and logged in the SCP database. The event was all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:38.080
but forgotten until December 23, 2016 when the&nbsp;
activity of SCP-1548 really began to pick up.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:45.120
On that day SCP-1548 began manifesting protection&nbsp;
symbols in rapid succession. Over the next few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:50.800
months a dense cloud of ionized gas formed around&nbsp;
the solar system. This ionized wall of radiation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:57.040
surrounded the heliopause, the boundary where the&nbsp;
sun’s radiation gives way to the vacuum of space.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:01.920
Over time this cloud became thicker, until&nbsp;
no light from outside of the solar system&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:06.880
could enter. Foundation censorship protocols&nbsp;
were quickly used to disseminate false data,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:11.440
suggesting that the solar system was passing&nbsp;
through a dense cloud of cosmic dust,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:16.000
and that was what was altering the night&nbsp;
sky and causing the stars to disappear

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:22.720
But as O5-6 continues to scan the files, he&nbsp;
knows what the true cause of this phenomenon is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:28.720
It must be SCP-1548. But why? Is the anomaly&nbsp;
trying to protect us from something outside of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:34.400
our solar system? Or is it trying to trap&nbsp;
humanity within, with no means of escape?

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:38.320
O5-6 stands up and stretches.&nbsp;
“That’s enough for today,”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:43.120
he says outloud to the empty room. He walks&nbsp;
towards the door and reaches for the handle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:48.880
All of a sudden sirens start going off and&nbsp;
red lights begin to flash. O5-6 spins around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:53.520
and runs back to the computer terminal. An&nbsp;
emergency alert begins coming through. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:57.760
Falcon Light5 rocket that launched earlier in&nbsp;
the day to bring supplies to the International&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:04.400
Space Station has spontaneously lost 50% of its&nbsp;
mass mid flight. O5-6 frantically begins typing;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:10.080
he brings up videos from surveillance satellites.&nbsp;
The Overseer watches in horror as pieces of debris&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:14.560
and bodies of the crew float through the&nbsp;
silence of space. The rocket looks like it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:20.400
has been cut directly down the middle, and half&nbsp;
of the structure has vanished from existence.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:24.000
What is happening? Suddenly another&nbsp;
alert comes in. All communication&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:28.000
has been lost with the International Space&nbsp;
Station. Without warning the space station&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:33.680
begins broadcasting a series of cognitohazards.&nbsp;
O5-6 quickly changes the channel to stop the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:38.080
signal from transmitting through his computer.&nbsp;
Reports start coming in from around the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:43.200
that anyone who continued listening to the&nbsp;
cognitohazard signals began entering trances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:46.480
then their brain completely&nbsp;
evaporated from their skulls.

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:50.000
There is a surge of thaumaturgic&nbsp;
particles in orbit around the Earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:58.560
O5-6 traces the particles back to their source.&nbsp;
They came from SCP-1548. The signal from the ISS&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:03.440
stops abruptly. The entire space station&nbsp;
changes course. It is on a trajectory to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:08.640
re-enter the Earth’s atmosphere. The friction&nbsp;
and heat will rip the space station apart.

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:14.560
O5-6 can’t believe what is happening. It&nbsp;
seems as if SCP-1548 helped humanity in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:20.320
a way by stopping the signals from the ISS.&nbsp;
But how can he be sure that SCP-1548 wasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:25.360
responsible for the cognitohazards in the&nbsp;
first place? He needs more information.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:31.200
O5-6 searches for answers as more anomalies&nbsp;
connected to SCP-1548 start occurring around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:36.160
the world. During a political demonstration&nbsp;
in Berlin, a thaumaturgic Way opens up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:41.360
that leads to a pocket dimension. Soon after&nbsp;
the appearance of the portal Koru Archpriest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:45.920
Farah Onteus, the leader of the Church of&nbsp;
the Second Hytoth, makes an announcement.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:51.280
He claims that the Way leads to a shelter, which&nbsp;
will protect people from the coming doom of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:55.760
universe. The people in the area, along with&nbsp;
members of the Church of the Second Hytoth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:59.440
make their way into the portal. Two&nbsp;
undercover Foundation agents follow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:05.600
the group. After everyone has entered, the Way&nbsp;
immediately closes, there is no further contact.

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:10.160
What does the Church of the Second&nbsp;
Hytoth know that we don’t? O5-6 wonders.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:15.760
He continues monitoring the situation and looking&nbsp;
for answers. Suddenly a message comes through all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:25.680
Foundation channels. It is coming from the sun.&nbsp;
It is not SCP-1548, instead, it is SCP-179,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:32.480
the humanoid permanently in space near the sun.&nbsp;
179 sends out one clear word in its signal:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:38.960
“defend.” Who is SCP-179 talking to?&nbsp;
O5-6 thinks. What needs to be defended?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:45.520
Is it humanity? Our solar system? The universe?
Another alarm begins to go off. “What now?”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:53.200
O5-6 screams. He brings up the alert; the screen&nbsp;
flashes to the moon. O5-6 focuses in on where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:59.120
the alert is coming from. It is a Foundation base&nbsp;
called Area-32. What remains left of the base is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:06.240
reporting that SCP-2821 suddenly expanded in size,&nbsp;
formed a wormhole that led to another region of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:12.800
the universe, and then vanished through it taking&nbsp;
38 Foundation members and 10 anomalies with it.&nbsp;

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:17.920
Sirens continue to go off. Distress signals&nbsp;
are being picked up on every channel. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:22.320
seems as if the world is coming to an&nbsp;
end, and everything that is happening is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:30.400
somehow connected to SCP-1548. A static filled&nbsp;
transmission begins coming in from SCP-3417.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:38.000
The words are urgent: “all Ortothans hear, all&nbsp;
Ortothans must listen now. The Stars are lost…”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:42.800
static breaks up the transmission for a few&nbsp;
moments before it resumes. “...Ago the First&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:48.400
Invasion occurred. The gods were unprepared,&nbsp;
never comprehending the fragility of the universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:55.440
after its creation. The worlds must fight—.” The&nbsp;
transmission cuts off. Everything goes silent.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:09:00.080
A pulsating SCP icon appears on&nbsp;
the screen of O5-6’s computer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:06.080
It is the part of the puzzle he has been waiting&nbsp;
for. In 1999 the O5 Council unanimously voted to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:11.040
launch a mission called Seraph-1 to explore&nbsp;
beyond the heliosphere, and the mission’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:16.640
true purpose was to explore the plausibility&nbsp;
of extraterrestrial SCP objects in space.&nbsp;

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:23.120
The message that O5-6 just received is from&nbsp;
Seraph-1; it is relaying information back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:29.280
Earth. The video shows the barrier of ionized&nbsp;
radiation that SCP-1548 had created glowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:34.240
orange at the border of the heliopause.&nbsp;
The radioactive wall seems to be made up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:41.600
of complex geometric patterns around 6,000 miles&nbsp;
across. Seraph-1 accelerates towards the barrier;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:47.120
it smashes through the protective shell.&nbsp;
The probe has entered interstellar space.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:52.800
O5-6 knows that everything he is seeing is on&nbsp;
a delay, as the information being sent back by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:58.560
Seraph-1 needs to travel vast distances, and it&nbsp;
takes significant time for the signals to reach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:04.320
Earth. After passing through the ionized&nbsp;
barrier the connection to Seraph-1 is lost.

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:09.120
Over the next few days O5-6 tries to&nbsp;
link the anomalies happening in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:15.680
solar system to SCP-1548. The Foundation&nbsp;
still hasn’t concluded if 1548 is harmful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:20.880
or trying to protect the solar system in some&nbsp;
way. Then a message comes in from Seraph-1;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.200
it has briefly regained communication with the&nbsp;
Foundation. Most of the probe’s instruments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:31.920
have been destroyed , but its rear facing camera&nbsp;
is still broadcasting. O5-6 pulls up the feed.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:37.440
He stares at the screen in horror as the images&nbsp;
unfold before him. The camera captures swarms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:42.800
of unknown entities surrounding the heliopause.&nbsp;
The bodies of the entities are asymmetrical with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:47.440
countless appendages and unknown structures&nbsp;
jutting out from their cores. They seem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:54.160
to range in size from 10 kilometers to 10,000&nbsp;
kilometers across. Although, some seem to be so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.160 --> 00:11:00.000
large that their size can only be hypothesized.
The swarms crash into the protective barrier that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:06.720
SCP-1548 has created around the solar system. Each&nbsp;
time part of the swarm rams the barrier thousands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:12.320
of thaumaturgic symbols and solar flares appear at&nbsp;
the point of impact. Two entities that are later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:20.320
classified as 1548-Ω-1 and 1548-Ω-2 are captured&nbsp;
entering the solar system by Seraph-1’s camera.&nbsp;

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:26.880
Video from Seraph-1 shows that as the probe exited&nbsp;
through the protective barrier it created a hole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:32.400
that remained open for a few moments. During&nbsp;
the time that the shield of ionized radiation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:42.640
was vulnerable 1548-Ω-1 and 1548-Ω-2 entered&nbsp;
through it. They are now inside the solar system.

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:47.760
SCP-1548 launches countermeasures in the&nbsp;
form of glowing red sigils that create&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:55.440
shockwaves to slow down Ω-1 and Ω-2. Ω-1 is&nbsp;
shaped like an eel with five contorted arms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.440 --> 00:12:00.400
radiating from its body, and a mouth&nbsp;
made of impossible geometric shapes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:06.000
Ω-2 has a tetrahedral structure that&nbsp;
leaves a trail of black rocks in its wake.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:12.320
As the two entities move towards the sun&nbsp;
SCP-1548 becomes more active. It closes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:17.600
hole in the barrier before any other creatures of&nbsp;
the swarm can enter, and then launches hundreds of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:24.400
concentrated blasts of thaumic energy at Ω-2. The&nbsp;
flares vaporize the entity in seconds. The last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:31.600
thing the video feed of Seraph-1 captures before&nbsp;
it cuts out is 1Ω-1 disappearing from view as it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:39.360
creeps towards the center of the solar system. It&nbsp;
has escaped the protective measures of SCP-1548.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:44.320
After the O5 Council reviews the footage&nbsp;
they decide to deploy the SCPS Curtana to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:49.760
intercept Ω-1. The orbital vessel is fully&nbsp;
equipped with experimental anomalous weapons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:55.520
and propulsion systems. The Council is sure&nbsp;
that the Curtana will be able to destroy Ω-1.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.520 --> 00:13:00.160
Data coming in from other satellites&nbsp;
indicate that Ω-1 has destroyed Pluto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:06.080
and other Kuiper Belt objects. It is slowly&nbsp;
making its way to the center of the solar system,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.080 --> 00:13:11.520
annihilating everything in its path.
The Curtana intercepts Ω-1 near Jupiter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:16.160
and engages the creature. After ten minutes&nbsp;
of battling, communication with the ship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:21.440
is lost. Probes in the area capture footage&nbsp;
of the Curtana and Ω-1 in mid battle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:26.560
when they are suddenly surrounded by a&nbsp;
black substance and both vanish from sight.

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:32.320
O5-6 and the other council members watch in&nbsp;
anticipation, unsure of what has just happened.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:39.040
Then the black substance dissipates. The SCPS&nbsp;
Curtana sits motionless in space. The entity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:44.880
is nowhere to be seen. A cheer erupts from the&nbsp;
Overseers and Foundation members in the room. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:51.120
seems the entity has been defeated. Then, without&nbsp;
warning, The Curtana accelerates rapidly. It is on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:56.400
a collision course with Mars. As the ship hurtles&nbsp;
past one of the probes in the asteroid belt the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.400 --> 00:14:02.240
Foundation members see an organic mass resembling&nbsp;
that of Ω-1 attached to the hull of the ship.

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:08.560
The Overseer Council watches in horror as&nbsp;
the SCPS Curtana smashes into the red planet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:14.720
leaving a crater 250 miles wide. The energy&nbsp;
released from the impact instantly ionizes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:19.920
the thin atmosphere of Mars, causing&nbsp;
the surface to turn into molten rock.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:25.760
From the epicenter of the impact crater a black&nbsp;
organic mass begins to crawl across the planet.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:29.840
The Overseers are frozen in fear, but SCP-1548&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:34.720
immediately deals with the entity&nbsp;
that is devouring the surface of Mars.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:41.840
From the sun comes the largest SCP-1548 instance&nbsp;
ever recorded. A solar flare is jettisoned towards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:48.080
Mars. The impact causes a fusion reaction&nbsp;
so intense, that for a moment, Mars shines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:54.480
as brightly as the sun. The planet explodes.&nbsp;
Its debris is cast across the solar system.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:59.040
Over time it will create a second asteroid&nbsp;
belt in the orbit that Mars once inhabited.

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:03.120
The Overseer Council is now convinced&nbsp;
that the threat has been dealt with.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:08.080
SCP-1548 is holding the swarm at&nbsp;
bay outside of the solar system,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:15.520
at least for the moment. O5-6 returns to his&nbsp;
office. He brings up the file on SCP-1548.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:23.280
He is still unsure of this SCP’s true intentions.&nbsp;
It seems to be protecting humanity, but why? O5-6&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:29.440
sits back in his chair and scrolls to the end of&nbsp;
the file; there is an update to the file by O5-3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:36.080
something that wasn’t there before. O5-6 opens&nbsp;
the new entry and reads the caption: “all that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:43.120
left of our infinite, ever expanding universe.”&nbsp;
O5-6 scrolls down. The image is a picture taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:49.600
by Sepaph-1 before contact was lost forever. It&nbsp;
is a picture of all that remains of the universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:55.520
There are two dots of light, and nothing else but&nbsp;
blackness. The swarm has destroyed everything in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.520 --> 00:16:02.400
the universe except for those two far away stars&nbsp;
and our own solar system which was protected by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:11.840
SCP-1548. But how long can it hold out, against&nbsp;
a universe destroying force. Only time will tell.

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:17.280
Now go check out SCP-2935 O Death and SCP-2000 for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:21.840
more tales of an apocalyptic&nbsp;
scale from the SCP Foundation.

